{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "initialState: data class x JSON value -> applied or rejected",
  "description": [
    "Shared vector for the app-side check that applies an initialState payload to a screen's Data (spec section 10.3).",
    "Run by: the three generators (sjui / kjui / rjui) through the code they emit, and the two libraries where they hold the check.",
    "Each case declares the screen's data (name and class exactly as a layout writes them) and an input object; expect lists the keys that are applied and the keys that are rejected with their reason.",
    "Compare applied and rejected as sets: order is not part of the contract.",
    "<class> in a reason is the class as the layout spells it, verbatim (Boolean stays Boolean, Int? keeps its ?).",
    "Order of the checks for one key: not a data field -> unsupported type -> null -> type. So an optional closure given null is still unsupported.",
    "The Android-only reason 'viewModel has no updateData' depends on the ViewModel, not on the value, and is not a case here."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "String <- \"a\"",
      "data": [
        {
          "name": "f",
          "class": "String"
        }
      ],
      "input": {
        "f": "a"
      },
      "expect": {
        "applied": [
          "f"
        ],
        "rejected": []
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "String <- \"\"",
      "data": [
        {
          "name": "f",
          "class": "String"
        }
      ],
      "input": {
        "f": ""
      },
      "expect": {
        "applied": [
          "f"
        ],
        "rejected": []
      }
    },
